; Hermetic guard suite for the smbc model parser.
;
; Every case replays a canned smbc answer through the fake solver, so the suite
; pins what nunchaku makes of a model it cannot fully read -- something no run
; against a real smbc can exercise on demand, because the interesting answers
; are the ones smbc emits rarely or not at all.  What each case is for is
; spelled out case by case in README.md; the manifest both that file and these
; rules are written against is cases.tsv.
;
; The four expectation words, and what a golden must therefore show:
;   recovered  the unknown gets a type and prints as `?__<n>`
;   opaque     no type is determined, and the output keeps `?__ ?name`
;   conflict   one identity at two types: exactly one warning, and every
;              occurrence printed as `?__unparsable <ty>`
;   contained  the entry is lost and the rest of the model is delivered, rc=0
;
; The rules are generated: they are all the same shape and cases.tsv is the
; single table, so gen_dune.ml reads it and dune.inc is promoted from that.
(include dune.inc)

(rule
 (targets dune.inc.gen)
 (deps
  (:gen gen_dune.ml)
  cases.tsv)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{targets}
   (run ocaml %{gen}))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff dune.inc dune.inc.gen)))
